# Security headers (Cloudflare). Based on the playbook's SECURITY-HEADERS template.
# CSP ships as Report-Only first (PRD §8); switch the header name to Content-Security-Policy once
# a deploy shows no violations. The sha256 below allow-lists the one inline script
# (src/lib/inline-scripts.ts); src/lib/headers.test.ts fails if they drift apart.
# X-Robots-Tag keeps the pre-launch site out of search; remove it at launch (PRD M3).

/*
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-Du+OJKJSbdUgz5nrHeWWINvez6XKDDU/tyj/5c2uvwo='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-XSS-Protection: 0
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
